From 37ed5ec77adcced03738b4b4b77177a57ab475c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Brocklehurst <matt@mattbrocklehurst.co.uk>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 01:34:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: bcm2837: add peripheral alias to dma-ranges for
 MMIO DMA

Same gap and same fix as bcm2836 (see that commit's message for the
full root-cause writeup, gdb-verified against QEMU's raspi2b machine).
bcm2837.dtsi's dma-ranges line is byte-for-byte identical to
bcm2836.dtsi's -- same single RAM-only entry, same missing peripheral
alias, so sdhost's own MMIO FIFO register (3f202000.mmc) hits the same
"no matching range" failure when DMA_ATTR_MMIO addresses get routed
through dev->dma_range_map.

Confirmed this is what real Raspberry Pi firmware itself patches in at
boot: dumped /proc/device-tree/soc/dma-ranges on a real Pi 3 Model B
(BCM2837) and found this exact second entry already present live,
byte-for-byte identical to this fix. Also documented as intentional,
first-party behavior in bcm2711.dtsi's emmc2bus node comment ("The
firmware will find whether the emmc2bus alias is defined, and if so,
it'll edit the dma-ranges property below accordingly") -- same
mechanism, different chip/controller.

Adds the same 0x3f000000 -> 0x7e000000 alias the sibling ranges
property (immediately above) already declares for CPU-side MMIO
access to the same peripherals.

Signed-off-by: Matt Brocklehurst <matt@mattbrocklehurst.co.uk>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2837.dtsi | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2837.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2837.dtsi
index c281697142b1..ba44cfb07668 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2837.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2837.dtsi
@@ -7,7 +7,8 @@ / {
 	soc {
 		ranges = <0x7e000000 0x3f000000 0x1000000>,
 			 <0x40000000 0x40000000 0x00001000>;
-		dma-ranges = <0xc0000000 0x00000000 0x3f000000>;
+		dma-ranges = <0xc0000000 0x00000000 0x3f000000>,
+			     <0x7e000000 0x3f000000 0x01000000>;
 
 		local_intc: interrupt-controller@40000000 {
 			compatible = "brcm,bcm2836-l1-intc";
-- 
